task: S89 T4 — History first segment starts at 00:00
requires: [FRONTEND_DEV]
sprint: S89

context: |
  useHistoryTimeline prints item.start as clock time. An overnight stop
  that began the previous day shows that earlier time as the first row.
  S87 selects the last segment on open and on date change. Keep that
  selection. This task only changes the first row's clock and duration.

steps:
  1. Pass the selected history date into useHistoryTimeline.
  2. For the first item only, if start is before local 00:00 of that date,
     show 00:00 and duration from 00:00 to item.end.
  3. Leave later rows on their own start times.
  4. Do not change the selectedEventIndex fallback (last item).

out:
  - src/screens/object-details/hooks/useHistoryTimeline.ts
  - src/screens/object-details/history/components/HistoryTabContainer.tsx

done:
  - Opening History and switching dates shows the first row at 00:00
    when the API start is earlier than that day.
  - The highlighted segment is still the last one.
  - A first segment that already starts after 00:00 is unchanged.
